\ Protocol-bounded dispatch on a satisfying operand under interpreter-free
\ AOT. A `bump-it` method is registered on the built-in `fixnum`, so fixnum
\ satisfies the `addable` protocol and the bounded call site dispatches to the
\ method. The method replays across the freeze->runtime boundary; if it did
\ not, the generic default body divides by zero and the binary exits non-zero.
\ A clean exit proves the replayed method ran. No virtual types or printing,
\ so the binary links no interpreter.

addable: protocol{ bump-it: } ;
bump-it: generic ( x: addable -- n ) [ 0 / ] ;
bump-it: method{ fixnum } [ 1 + ] ;

5 bump-it drop
